# Docker does not read .gitignore, so without this `COPY . /build` ships the
# host's build tree into the image.
#
# That is not merely wasteful. ng/build holds a CMakeCache.txt recording the
# absolute path it was generated in, and cmake refuses to reuse a cache from a
# different directory -- so `docker build .` failed outright on any machine
# where ng had been built locally first, which is the normal order of work. CI
# never saw it because CI starts from a fresh checkout.
#
# The autotools .am/.in sources and the generated `configure` are tracked and
# must reach the image; only their build-time output is excluded here.

.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude

# autotools output
Makefile
config.h
config.log
config.status
stamp-h1
autom4te.cache/
src/Makefile
src/.deps/
src/*.o
src/slowhttptest
man/Makefile

# cmake output
ng/Makefile
ng/build/
ng/build-*/

# editor and OS leavings
*~
.DS_Store
